{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1352648-unstoppable-sunfire-prominence-does-it-increase-hardness","id":1352648,"title":"Unstoppable Sunfire Prominence, does it increase hardness?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-04T11:11:27-08:00","id":1352648,"title":"Unstoppable Sunfire Prominence, does it increase hardness?","content":"Its the Charm from Arms of the chosen, All conquering collosus warstrider page 144.<br /> I am asking because of the rule tha says hardness doesn't stack. However this is an increase of hardness so I am a bit confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2024-malfi","name":"Malfi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T11:24:52-08:00","id":1352652,"title":"","content":"I think the interpretation that makes the most sense in this case is that it does increase your Hardness, yes. It's worded as &quot;+1 Hardness&quot;, implying it's adding to something, and the way the mechanics work, if it <i>didn't</i> stack, it would be almost useless as a charm - the warstrider by itself has Hardness 12, so you'd have to burn at least 13 initiative to get even one past that, and you'd have to roll 13 or more successes on your initiative, or, more likely, <i>half</i> your initiative, even to be able to spend that much. That's pretty harsh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T18:30:32-08:00","id":1352718,"title":"","content":"This Warstrider's defensive powers are based mainly on stacking great amounts of Hardness together, so yeah, it's an exception","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T22:09:30-08:00","id":1352734,"title":"","content":"Although hardness from multiple sources doesn't stack as a general rule, I think it's reasonable to consider the hardness from an artifact armor and a hardness increase from that same armor's Evocations to be a single source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T01:16:56-08:00","id":1352772,"title":"","content":"I guess it stacks then.<br /> Many thanks to everyone for responding!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2024-malfi","name":"Malfi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}